00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:05.349 align:start position:0%
as a company that specializes in big  data analysis and integration  it has always been our passion to make  bioinformatics  more accessible we already have a  platform for learning about  bioinformatics in the context of a  project-based curriculum  but previously we downplayed the  importance of coding  in part it was due to the fact that many  biologists just don't have the time  to learn a new skill and in part it was  due to the challenges  in getting the initial setup steps and  technical issues  out of the way remotely but we soon  discovered that this is  only a part of the full solution to  close the data science gap for  non-engineers  we have to focus on all of the central  issues  that will enable anyone to be effective  at managing processing analyzing  and integrating large data that is why  today we are launching  the omics logic code playground here we  will be posting  practical coding assignments that will  help you  understand the r and python code syntax  for common types of tasks  a bioinformatician faces in day-to-day  work  as a result you will learn how to  process genomic  transcriptomic and meta-genomic data on  the cloud or dedicated high-performance  computing server stack  by launching processing pipelines that  structure and prepare data for  downstream  analysis these tasks can be easily  automated and mastered  on the tbinfo platform which offers a  streamlined process  from learning to the application of  bioinformatics and life sciences  but as soon as the data is processed the  work of a data scientist begins  you have to explore understand and  wrangle multiple tables and data frames  to find patterns  and annotate them with biological  meaning that is why in the code  playground you will find  course collections on genomics  transcriptomics  metagenomics and data science in each  course you will load transform and  visualize data  in r or python from single bar plots to  complex multi-dimensionality reduction  techniques like principle component  analysis  or clustering for data mining including  classification  and regression that will allow you to  group data objects by feature similarity  and train machine learning models for  predictive analysis  not only will you learn about the  methods you will also understand them by  applying the analysis to your own data  sets  and modifying settings to see how each  line of code  contains important instructions to  transform a  complex data set into a fascinating  discovery  from the very basics to the cutting edge  loading transformation visualization as  well as discovery of  patterns and real data sets used by  researchers to study and understand  biological phenomena at the molecular  level now code playground is a part of  our  immersive omixlogic programs where we  combine online interactive sessions  self-guided study materials and  practical assignments using the tbi info  platform  and the coding challenges in both r and  python  so get started today at  code.omicslogic.com
 

